-- Sets up "What Undoing Really Means" (Unit 1, A.2) as a scannable packet:
-- one packet version, its rubric, and the 32 answer-box anchors the scan
-- pipeline crops against. A.2 is the second packet to get this treatment;
-- A.1 (packet version 1462a2f2) is the working precedent and every
-- convention below is taken from it.
--
-- Geometry comes from the distributed print master
-- (U1_A2_What_Undoing_Really_Means.pdf, 20 pages, A4), read with the same
-- filled-rectangle detection the A.1 anchors came from
-- (platform/scripts/inspect_fillrects.py). Answer boxes are drawn at
-- x0=50.83/x1=544.50; the packet's information boxes (WHAT YOU NEED, TOK,
-- ATL, spotlights) are drawn at the inset 51.02/544.25 and quote boxes at
-- 87.87/466.93, which is what separates the 32 answer boxes from the 25
-- decorative ones. Every anchor was rendered over its page and checked by
-- eye before this migration was written.
--
-- Printed question numbers are NOT the parts[] ordinal: the Part 0 Desmos
-- activity occupies parts[] slot 2 but is printed unnumbered, so printed
-- Qn == parts[] question n+1 from Q2 onwards. That mapping was verified
-- against all 21 printed "Clev's Marks: N" labels -- all 21 agree with the
-- parts[] marks exactly. page_count is 20, the length of the distributed
-- PDF, matching how A.1 records 26 for a document whose own footer says 32:
-- the Extension section is generated but not printed, and page_count is the
-- stride the batch segmenter uses to find where each student's copy starts.

values ('2f8a4c31-6b7e-4d92-a1f5-8c3e07b9d240', '41e8ca4e-087d-4146-b364-19139d659343', 'A.2 v1 (print master)', 20, 'auto_fillrect', true);

-- One rubric row per answer box, not per question: a sub-part with its own
-- printed box gets its own editable entry (A.1's convention). question_text
-- and answer_key are scoped to that box's own sub-parts, so the assessor is
-- never shown a neighbouring box's prompt and left to discard it -- the
-- failure that produced A.1's Q1/Q1(e) backtracking (HANDOFF open item 4c).
-- source is 'authored_from_print' rather than 'generated' deliberately:
-- lib/na-rubric-bridge.ts keys on the parts[] ordinal, which is off by one
-- from the printed numbering here, and it skips any row whose source is not
-- 'generated' -- so this marker is what stops a later packet re-save from
-- overwriting these rows with differently-numbered ones.

-- The Part 0 Desmos box carries no marks and no key of any kind, which is
-- exactly what lib/na-assessment.ts's isUngradedAnchor() looks for: stage 5
-- skips it rather than inventing a verdict for a thinking space.
--
-- expand_max_y1_pt stops each crop just short of the next printed box on the
-- page (4pt clear), or at 811.89 -- the last baseline above the footer --
-- when the box is last on its page. Q19's reflection table is ruled, not
-- filled, so only its header row registers as a fill-rect; its anchor is
-- drawn manually over the whole table (255.82-470.00, five body rows ending
-- at the 465.9 rule), the same manual_table treatment A.1's Q9 needed.
